 "_": [
  "Committee YouTube channels. A CONGRESS-ONLY artefact, and it says so here so",
  "nobody wonders why New York's 82 committees are absent: official channels",
  "exist for federal committees and essentially not for state ones. 31 of the 34",
  "full committees on our record are mapped; subcommittees run no channels and",
  "are not tried.",
  "",
  "Built by one discovery pass (scripts/agents/discover-committee-youtube.py) and",
  "then decided BY HAND, because the automated pass was wrong four times: a",
  "YouTube search for a federal committee ranks VERMONT's legislature above it, so",
  "'Vermont Senate Committee on Finance' came back for Senate Finance and three",
  "more like it. Handle-guessing was worse \u2014 @HouseTransportation is a moving",
  "company in Medina and @WaysAndMeans is a person. A search hit is not a",
  "verification; every entry below was read before it was written.",
  "",
  "Three committees are deliberately absent rather than wrong: Senate Agriculture",
  "and Senate Rules have no channel of their own, and Senate Homeland Security",
  "resolves to the HOUSE committee's channel, which would be a lie about both.",
  "",
  "Many committees run MAJORITY or MINORITY channels rather than one institutional",
  "one ('House Judiciary GOP', 'Senate Energy Dems'), so the title is kept beside",
  "the id: what the card shows is that channel's latest hearing, not the",
  "committee's, and the title is how a reader can tell.",
  "",
  "`uploads` is the channel's uploads playlist. Reading it costs ONE quota unit",
  "against playlistItems.list; the search that found these cost 100 each, which is",
  "why finding is a build step and showing is not."
 ],
